id: pm-ado-sdk-adoption
title: Use SDK settings-aware item reads and guarded sync persistence
description: "Adopt both unused SDK capabilities from the 2026-10-25 audit: settings-aware locateItem and commitItemMutations match preconditions. Preserve raw-document hashes and ordinary sync output; prove configured lookup and concurrent-write refusal with real non-git trackers, origin/main differential evidence and behavioural revert tests."
type: Chore
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[2]: refactor,sdk-adoption
created_at: "2026-10-25T16:11:56.608Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-25T16:15:34.694Z"
assignee: codex-agent
claim_principal: codex-agent
author: codex-agent
parent: pm-ado-g4v1
comments[8]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-25T15:50:43.902Z",codex-agent,"Orientation found no existing SDK-adoption item. Related SDK certification: pm-ado-qq1p; source features: pm-ado-4x3u and pm-ado-nc7z. Both audited SDK APIs exist in the pinned 2026.10.23 dependency. Plan: preserve authoritative raw documents, replace unguarded sync persistence with inspected-snapshot match preconditions, run non-git regression/differential/revert proofs and unchanged npm/Bun release gates."
  "2026-10-25T15:57:29.077Z",codex-agent,"Both replacements implemented. Resolution passes readSettings item_format and resolveItemTypeRegistry type_to_folder into locateItem and retains readLocatedItem whole-document hashing. Sync now uses commitItemMutations update match on inspected updated_at for link, relation and base writes. Expected revisions advance from our own immutable SDK transaction history, never from a refreshed current item. Three new real non-git regressions pass: custom nested folder/raw-document guard, local edit after Azure PATCH, and local edit before import relation/base persistence. The last two preserve the concurrent item/history bytes and return ADO_CONFLICT; remote success can remain partial."
  "2026-10-25T16:01:16.414Z",codex-agent,"Compatibility check found SDK gap tracked by pm-ado-sdk-match-close-1025: match on updated_at also runs inside update's internal terminal close after its first write has advanced the timestamp. Workaround uses one SDK transaction with a guarded scalar update then explicit close. SDK history messages necessarily become bulk-item-transaction markers instead of adapter prose; this intentional diagnostic difference is documented and differential-tested. Initial read-only differential passed over public pm-ado and pm-jira origin snapshots: 140 items, 8 exact output comparisons, unchanged authoritative bytes. Extending proof to writable copies for persistence receipts, values and history patches."
  "2026-10-25T16:03:28.536Z",codex-agent,"Revert proof, lookup: restored only AdoResolutionService.document from origin/main, rebuilt dist, then node --test --test-name-pattern='SDK lookup' test/sync.test.ts failed 1/1 as expected (custom nested folder scope refusal). Revert proof, sync: replaced only the local update helper with ordinary pm.update, rebuilt dist, then node --test --test-name-pattern='SDK sync match' test/sync.test.ts failed 2/2 as expected (newer local edits overwritten / success instead of conflict). Restored both implementations and rebuilt: all 4 targeted tests pass, including terminal lifecycle compatibility. No history records were rewritten."
  "2026-10-25T16:03:30.848Z",codex-agent,"Differential PASS: origin/main 7f44a1d build versus candidate, public pm-ado 7f44a1d (32 items) and pm-jira 2fd1537 (108 items). Four exact read-only outputs per corpus: import/export/sync dry-run and resolution plan, unchanged authoritative bytes. Three writable-copy persistence projections per corpus: actual import receipt, final metadata excluding updated_at, history op/author/patch excluding updated_at; history lengths equal. Total 14 comparisons over 140 real items. Only intentional difference in ordinary writes is mandatory SDK transaction history messages; both old/new forms asserted. Full method and reproducible command in docs/sdk-adoption.md."
  "2026-10-25T16:05:59.894Z",codex-agent,"Targeted compatibility checks passed 7/7. The first full gate ran 229/229 tests successfully but correctly rejected uncovered SDK error propagation (100% thresholds unchanged). Added a real-tracker regression for invalid mapped state and unusable transaction storage, plus explicit/unknown author attribution; it passes 1/1. Pinned pm linked tests passed 2/2 (typecheck and 4 targeted regressions); test-result tracking is disabled by existing project policy, so run output was inspected and results recorded here. Isolated-identity strict health passes. Normal host health exposes an unrelated global pm-github host-version skew; no global config was changed."
  "2026-10-25T16:09:54.868Z",codex-agent,"Local npm full gate PASS: env HOME=an isolated home GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL=/dev/null GIT_CONFIG_NOSYSTEM=1 npm run release:check (the HOME expression here is descriptive only; run used an isolated home). Both the V8 pass and independent statement-instrumented pass ran 230/230 tests, 0 failures/skips. All 8 required source files covered; 1380/1380 statements, 100% lines/branches/functions; docstrings 90/90 declarations, production audit zero vulnerabilities, build/typecheck/pack/changelog/publish-attestation/date checks passed. git diff --check clean. No standalone lint script exists in this repository; its configured docstring gate passed. Bun full gate is running."
  "2026-10-25T16:15:34.693Z",codex-agent,"Local full gates PASS: env HOME=\"$(mktemp -d)\" GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL=/dev/null GIT_CONFIG_NOSYSTEM=1 npm run release:check; the same isolated identity with bun run release:check also passes. Each gate runs 230/230 tests in both V8 and independent statement-instrumented passes, with zero failures/skips. Coverage: 1380/1380 statements and 100% lines/branches/functions across 8 sources. Typecheck/build, 90/90 documented declarations, production audit zero vulnerabilities, pack/changelog/attestation/date checks pass. Pinned pm linked tests rerun on this item: 2/2 pass. Public text privacy scan and git diff --check pass. No standalone lint script is configured. Ready for PR CI; no merge or release authorized."
